+Nesting depth is the one position fact that does *not* normalise away. The
+braced-body cap (`E207`) counts nesting from the top of the document, so each
+deferred body records the depth the shell found it at
+(`DeferredBody::body_depth`), the isolated walk starts from it, and it is part
+of `ItemBodyKey` (packed into `body_env`). A body moved to another nesting depth
+is a cache miss, which is rare. A body that passes the cap reports the same
+`E207` as the whole-file walk, which sends the document down the
+`ErrorDiagnostic` fallback, so a grafted scope tree is never deeper than the
+whole-file one.
